CON-07: subtract only pervious-surface evaporation from the GW ET budget

RunoffSolver::execute() reproduced legacy's `if (i == PERV) Vpevap += Vevap;`,
which adds the running total of all three subareas' surface evaporation, so
water evaporating from the impervious surface took ET away from the
aquifer. Vol I eq. 5-11/5-12 subtract only the pervious surface's
evaporation. Add only the pervious subarea's own evaporation, as
CON-07_swmm530.patch does for 5.3.0.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-07_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/hydrology/Runoff.cpp b/src/engine/hydrology/Runoff.cpp
index aa81dc7..80bd07c 100644
--- a/src/engine/hydrology/Runoff.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/hydrology/Runoff.cpp
@@ -473,14 +473,9 @@ void RunoffSolver::execute(SimulationContext& ctx, double dt, double evap_rate_i
 
             // Step 3.5: Update mass balance volumes (legacy lines 934-937)
             Vevap  += surfEvap * subarea_area * dt;
-            // legacy subcatch.c:984 `if (i == PERV) Vpevap += Vevap;` — the
-            // WHOLE subcatchment's surface evaporation so far (the pervious
-            // subarea is processed last, after both impervious ones), not
-            // the pervious share. gwater_getGroundwater subtracts it from
-            // MaxEvap = Evap.rate * FracPerv, so an impervious cover
-            // evaporating at the full rate leaves the aquifer no evaporation
-            // (runoff41-sw5: legacy's soil moisture holds at field capacity).
-            if (isPervious) Vpevap += Vevap;
+            // Only the pervious subarea's surface evaporation is subtracted
+            // from the aquifer's ET budget (Vol I eq. 5-11/5-12).
+            if (isPervious) Vpevap += surfEvap * subarea_area * dt;
             Vinfil += infil * subarea_area * dt;
 
             // Step 3.6: Loss check shortcut (legacy lines 945-948)
